INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(618,'https://aiforgood.itu.int/trust-isnt-coded-it-must-be-designed-into-the-ecosystem/','https://aiforgood.itu.int/trust-isnt-coded-it-must-be-designed-into-the-ecosystem','Trust isn’t coded – it must be designed into the ecosystem','trustisntcoded','itu_ai4good','ITU AI for Good','en','2026-10-12T12:00:36Z','2026-10-17T08:55:20Z','AI may be powered by code, but its ability to create sustained value for people depends on the ecosystems built around it. As AI moves from experimentation to scale, trust must become a system capability – connecting data, governance, operational oversight and partnerships across institutional boundaries. The post Trust isn’t coded – it must be designed into the ecosystem appeared first on AI for Good .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(619,'https://aiforgood.itu.int/why-we-were-at-ai-for-good-grounding-artificial-intelligence-in-knowledge-you-can-trust/','https://aiforgood.itu.int/why-we-were-at-ai-for-good-grounding-artificial-intelligence-in-knowledge-you-can-trust','Why we were at AI for Good: grounding artificial intelligence in knowledge you can trust','whywewereataiforgoodgroundingartificialintelligenceinknowledgeyoucantrust','itu_ai4good','ITU AI for Good','en','2026-10-09T12:00:44Z','2026-10-17T08:55:20Z','Ask anyone building or using AI tools for research what their biggest concerns are, and hallucinations and citation problems come up fast. In fact, 64% of researchers cited potential inaccuracies and hallucinations as concerns preventing them using AI as much as they''d like in our global study. The more urgent question is how quickly institutions can adapt to realize AI’s benefits – and expand their capacity to improve lives. The post Why we were at AI for Good: grounding artificial intelligence in knowledge you can trust appeared first on AI for Good .',2.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
